@startuml uml-activity-job-handling
title Job handling — UML activity diagram

start
:Receive job (push endpoint / poll worker);
:PEP 1 — authenticate requester;\nvalidate payload (SHACL);
if (active agreement referenced?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Match request × offers\n+ station policy (PDP);
  if (match found?) then (yes)
    if (approval required?) then (yes)
      :Create agreement (pending-approval);\nnotify data controller; await decision;
      if (approved?) then (yes)
      else (no)
        :Reject job / request; record in audit log;
        stop
      endif
    else (no — auto)
    endif
    :Activate + sign agreement; share with train;
  else (no)
    :Reject job / request; record in audit log;
    stop
  endif
endif
:Enqueue job;
:PEP 2 — pre-execution check\n(agreement · station policy · quotas);
if (permit?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Reject job; record in audit log;
  stop
endif
:Execute via mechanism adapter (isolated);
:Collect results;\nPEP 3 — result & obligation check;
:Deliver results;\nschedule post-execution obligations;
stop

note right
  Every checkpoint decision, state change
  and execution emits an audit event
  linked to the governing agreement.
end note
@enduml
